# Build context exclusions.
#
# Phase 20: the original patterns were root-anchored only. Docker matches
# a pattern like `node_modules` against the context-root path alone, so
# `apps/api/node_modules` and `apps/api/.env` were being SENT to the
# builder and copied by `COPY apps/api ./apps/api`. Nested paths therefore
# need `**/` prefixes. This mattered twice over: a symlinked host
# node_modules tree cannot be used inside the image, and a real .env
# (with a DATABASE_URL) must never enter an image build.

# Dependencies and build output (always regenerated inside the image).
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.expo
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS and tooling metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Secrets — never send real env files to the daemon. `.env.example`
# templates contain no secrets and are kept out too, so nothing in the
# image can accidentally be treated as configuration.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/.env.*
**/.envrc

# Local document storage (STORAGE_DIR) must be mounted, never baked in.
# NOTE: only the `uploads` directories are local document storage.
# `apps/api/src/storage/` is source code and must NOT be excluded.
**/uploads

# Logs and editor scratch files.
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# Local databases / scratch data.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
